Chrome browser themes for {{ theme.name }}. {{ theme.description }}

## Installation
{% if adapter.mirror %}
Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/{{ adapter.mirror }}.git
```
{% endif %}{% for v in variants %}
### {{ v.variant.name }} Theme

{{ v.variant.description }}

1. Open `chrome://extensions/` in Chrome
2. Enable "Developer mode" in the top right
3. Click "Load unpacked"
4. Select the `{% if adapter.mirror %}{{ repo }}/{% endif %}{{ theme.id }}-{{ v.variant.id }}/` directory

**Key colors:** {{ v.variant.appearance | capitalize }} backgrounds ({{ v.base.background }}) with active tabs ({{ v.roles.ui.accent }})
{% endfor %}
## Notes

- Due to Chrome manifest v3 limitations, customizable elements are limited
- For more detailed color control, consider using CSS extension tools like Stylus
- Only one theme can be active at a time
